    "result": "Perfect! The fix is working correctly. Both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are now created when running `frai gate init --ci` through the frai CLI.\n\n**Summary of the fix:**\n\nThe bug was in `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` at the `gate` command handler. The issue was that Commander's variadic argument handling (`[args...]`) only captures positional arguments, not flags. When passing arguments to the spawned `frai-gate` process, the `--ci` flag was being lost.\n\nThe fix reconstructs the arguments from `process.argv` directly, which includes both positional arguments and flags. This ensures all command-line arguments are correctly passed through to the `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n**Changes made:**\n- Modified the `gate` command action handler to use `process.argv` to capture all arguments including flags\n- Now properly passes `--ci` and other flags to the spawned `frai-gate` process\n- Rebuilt the frai package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- Tested and confirmed the workflow file is now created correctly",
